{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/783058-interpretation-of-the-mechanics-of-the-lair","id":783058,"title":"Interpretation of the Mechanics of the Lair","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-09T14:41:19-08:00","id":783058,"title":"Interpretation of the Mechanics of the Lair","content":"The Primordial Pathways rules and their related mechanics are a bit of a personal obsession of mine when it comes to Beast, so I figured I'd try to get my thoughts and speculation down in writing. Open to discussion for the sake of refining understanding and the like.<br /> <br /> <b>Beasts can only open Primordial Pathways to locations that are of the same basic location-type as one of their Chambers.</b> Temporary Pathways lack the flexibility and adaptive nature of Burrows, so they tend to link deserts to deserts, houses to houses, forests to forests, and so on. This tends to make Chambers culled from distant or abstracted parts of the cosmology less useful for resonance, but the remoteness of those locations and the scarcity of Chamber slots tends to mean one doesn't go to the trouble of incorporating them without a strong incentive.<br /> <br /> <b>The penalties for dissimilarity apply to substitute locations for the purposes of opening Pathways and imposing Lair Traits from scratch, but &quot;upgrading&quot; has no expiration date.</b> What this means in the grand scheme of things is that Beasts who intend to use the substitution method often are incentivized to witness breaking points or use Nightmares in the same sorts of locations as comprise their Chambers, thus spreading the influence of their Legend as a means of making inroads for broadening connections to their Lair.<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Shortcuts&quot; like Under the Bed or Skeleton Key are less stringent than regular Pathways.</b> Under the Bed takes a Beast to whichever Chamber their Horror currently dwells in, since the connection works from any location with a marked mortal and can only transport the Beast themself. Using Skeleton Key to connect a gateway to the Primordial Dream produces an effect similar to a Burrow, linking the doorway to a Chamber of the Beast's choice (which probably varies by Satiety to account for the merging with the Horror that typically still occurs).<br /> <br /> <b>Burrows need not adhere to the Chamber's original topology.</b> Doors that don't exist in a house-Chamber's physical counterpart can lead to other Chambers, as can pits and pools and pathways and sundry other portals that one might find. This is important chiefly for the purposes of using conventional Primordial Pathways to access the Lair for longer than a few turns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}